   "solution": "Drop from the western overlook onto the broad middle pressure shelf. Walk to its right end so Oren has genuinely followed the route onto the shelf, then press the companion action to hold him there. His weight keeps the central pier open. Drop down beside the visible tally curtain and cross through the open pier along the lower gallery to the east tally; it opens the exit and upper curtain. Return onto the recoil plate near the pier. Call Oren onward: leaving his plate closes the pier, which is now the missing climbing wall. Fully compress the recoil plate, release Down, jump left as it rises, then Updash beside the restored wall and hold Jump for a wallbounce. Land on the broad one-way middle rest. Jump/dash back toward the pier, climb its right side and hop onto its top. Take the upper shelf west and make the ordinary final jump onto the original overlook.",
   "nearestExisting": "F19 asks that a weight stay while the knight leaves, and F34 makes a wall useful only in one machinery state. B39 (Borrow Only Enough) supplies the compress–release–jump timing of the recoil platform. Here the helper must first copy a real descent to a distant plate, then be explicitly called off it after the lower crossing. The same central pier changes from obstruction to open passage to recoil-assisted wallbounce face to upper return support.",
   "novelty": "Oren cannot be placed remotely or teleported: the knight authors the helper path before requesting the hold. Keeping the convenient passage open is exactly what prevents the return launch. The east tally opens a visibly gated upper approach, preventing an initial hop over the helper puzzle; the pier’s west teeth prevent climbing the outbound side. The useful new recoil platform and late wallbounce only work together after the old companion interaction changes shared geometry.",
