   "interconnection": "The mould stands in the outgoing shot line and the returning watch-light line. One distant coil opens the exit beside the starting station and releases the lower carrier. The carrier delivers the knight to the anvil beyond the thorn field; that anvil reaches the high return gallery, which drops onto the windward casting face. The final gust returns to the original parry platform and home door.",
   "superroom": {
    "screenAreas": 3.756521739130435,
    "stages": [
     "Send a bolt upwind through the empty screen",
     "Ride under the shared firing lane to the far anvil",
     "Return above the thorns into the casting pocket",
     "Cast the screen and ride the gale home"
    ],
    "scaleNote": "One continuous 96×36 room. The route travels from the centre to the far right, rises to the high gallery, descends to the shared frame, and returns across the original station to the far-left exit."
   },
   "requiredEventCounts": {
    "cast": 3
   },
   "route": {
    "exited": true,
    "frames": 966,
    "deaths": 0
   },
   "endingForgiveness": "The rope-height changes each have a six-tile transition gap; four-frame earlier and later payout variants pass. The receiving shelf is six tiles wide and allows a normal climb to the anvil. The casting pocket gains a visible rear guard with the same cut, preventing a late bolt from making the ending depend on arrival phase. A three-second rest behind the completed screen passes.",
   "designNotes": "Only B52 opts into watchClarity presentation. The roof leaves eight pixels over the carrier—enough for the deck but not the knight. Alternating floor/hanging/floor teeth make rope length consequential. The original top-riding tape and fixed-rope alternatives fail. Grab is remappable: hold Grab; Up reels in; Down pays out; Jump releases. Added one visible mould cell in the casting pocket to shelter the delayed final jump from later shots.",
